  "id": "Compound::DB00398 - Gene::1559",
  "verbalization": "Sorafenib is implicated in the pathogenesis of Drug-induced Liver Injury (DILI), which is mediated through a chain of events involving Cyp2c9. The evidence suggests that Sorafenib may inhibit Cyp2c9, as it is linked to DILI through Pioglitazone, which binds to Cyp2c9 and is a known inducer of liver injury. Similarly, Sorafenib is associated with Hepatic Pain, which is caused by Anastrozole, another compound that binds to Cyp2c9. These findings collectively indicate that Sorafenib may act as a modulator of Cyp2c9, potentially through inhibition or induction, depending on the context. The shared pathway involving Cyp2c9 across different drug-induced liver injury mechanisms underscores a possible role for Sorafenib in the regulation of Cyp2c9 activity. The integration of these findings supports a mechanistic link between Sorafenib and Cyp2c9, particularly in the context of liver injury, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
